<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wangen im Allgäu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wangen im <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allgau">Allgäu</a> is a town in the Allgäu region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> which grew from a settlement under the Abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a> and became a free imperial city in the 13th century. It remained Catholic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>, passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1802 and to Württemberg in 1810, and keeps a well-preserved old town with painted gate towers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wangen-im-allgau.jpg" alt="Wangen im Allgäu" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Lorer · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wangen_i_a_air16.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
